<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">20072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>US Central Command has opened a ninth straight day of strikes on Iran's coastal defences, and Iran's Revolutionary Guard has answered by hitting American bases in Kuwait and Jordan.</s> <s>Seventeen US troops have died since the war began, in an operation first sold as a limited mission to keep oil moving through the Strait of Hormuz.</s> <s>With the strait now closed and Brent crude above ninety dollars a barrel, a campaign to protect shipping has become an open-ended war.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>South Africa's suspended inspector general of intelligence, Imtiaz Fazel, has told the high court that the former police minister's office engineered his removal.</s> <s>Fazel was probing irregular spy-agency procurement, including a covert hotel purchase, when his oversight powers were stripped away.</s> <s>His case asks a hard question — what protects a democracy when the watchdog of its security services can be silenced by the very ministers he's meant to watch.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Venezuela's death toll from June's twin earthquakes has climbed to five thousand two hundred and eight, with nearly eighteen thousand people left homeless.</s> <s>The National Assembly's daily count also lists sixteen thousand injured as more than a thousand aftershocks keep striking Yaracuy state.</s> <s>A sanctioned, cash-starved government now faces one of the year's deadliest disasters with an emergency system already hollowed out.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Norway has unveiled a memorial naming all seventy-seven people killed by the neo-Nazi Anders Breivik, days before the attack's fifteenth anniversary.</s> <s>He set off a car bomb in Oslo and then shot sixty-nine more, most of them teenagers, at a summer camp on Utoya island in twenty eleven.</s> <s>The country chose to remember each victim by name just as the anti-immigrant politics that drove him hardens again across Europe.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A standoff in the northern province of Badakhshan has exposed the limits of Taliban rule five years after it seized power.</s> <s>Afghanistan's rulers still lean on local commanders rather than a central administration, and Kabul's writ fades quickly beyond the capital.</s> <s>Winning territory, it turns out, is far easier than governing it — collecting taxes, delivering services, and commanding loyalty.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Five sailors were killed and five more are missing after Russian cruise missiles struck the Golden Leo, a Turkish-owned grain carrier flagged to Guinea-Bissau, off the port of Odessa.</s> <s>The ship was leaving Ukraine's export corridor when three missiles found it.</s> <s>Striking a civilian vessel crewed by neutral nationals attacks both the law protecting merchant shipping and the food supply of importers far from the front.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Two of Israel's most senior ministers, Bezalel Smotrich and Itamar Ben-Gvir, marched to the Gaza fence demanding the rebuilding of settlements evacuated in two thousand five.</s> <s>Prime Minister Netanyahu's own party sponsored the Nachala-organised march.</s> <s>What was once a fringe cause now carries cabinet endorsement, testing how far the return to Gaza has moved into the political mainstream.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China bought nearly twenty-eight percent more Russian liquefied natural gas in the first half of this year, yet paid only about eight percent more for it.</s> <s>That widening gap between volume and value is the sanctions story in a single number — Beijing is absorbing the gas the West shunned, at a steep discount.</s> <s>Western measures didn't stop Russia's energy trade so much as redirect it eastward, and cheaply.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria will soon require miners to hold a digital identity linked to the national register, after enforcement teams arrested more than three hundred suspected illegal operators.</s> <s>The mining minister says tying licences to verified identities is meant to choke off the cash that funds armed groups across the country's north.</s> <s>Whether a database can reach the well-connected, or only the small-scale digger, remains the open question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Egypt has created a sovereign fund whose assets grow through presidential decrees transferring state property, and which answers to a private board rather than parliament.</s> <s>Lawmakers had already stripped a bond clause meant to shield the finance ministry's authority.</s> <s>A fund accountable only to the president quietly moves public wealth beyond the reach of the people's representatives.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A deep-water coral reef off Benin, written off as dead in nineteen-sixties fishing surveys, has been found alive and healthy.</s> <s>Sonar and a deep-sea camera system revealed that six decades of assumption, never once a survey, had buried a thriving ecosystem.</s> <s>Most of Africa's deep-sea coral remains completely unmapped, which means other reefs declared dead may simply be waiting to be looked at.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Five people died when adobe houses collapsed in a magnitude five point five earthquake near Sicaya, in Peru's central highlands.</s> <s>Officials say traditional mud-brick construction worsened the damage and displaced three hundred residents.</s> <s>The same material that keeps homes cool in the Andes turns deadly when the ground shakes — a poverty of engineering, not of warning.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>About one hundred and fifty polar bear hides are sold legally each year for some sixty thousand dollars apiece, a trade the global wildlife convention still labels sustainable.</s> <s>Canada has twice defended that designation against calls for tighter protection.</s> <s>With only twenty-two to thirty-one thousand bears left, campaigners are pressing to move the species onto a stricter list before the maths turns against it.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Twenty nations sent one hundred warplanes and two thousand five hundred personnel to bases across northern Australia for the biennial Exercise Pitch Black.</s> <s>Prime Minister Albanese calls the three-week drills proof of deepening security partnerships.</s> <s>As the Indo-Pacific militarises, joint exercises have become the region's main language of deterrence — rehearsing a war in the hope of never fighting one.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Samsung has cut seven hundred and thirty-nine consumer-electronics jobs in the United States as it moves the unit's headquarters to Texas.</s> <s>South Korea's electronics giant is chasing lower taxes and proximity to its new chip plant, clustering research beside manufacturing.</s> <s>It's the same magnetic pull reshaping the industry — talent and factories drawn together, and the workers who won't relocate left behind.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Anthropic's Claude Code, the widely used AI coding assistant, has quietly shifted onto Bun, a JavaScript runtime whose core is written in the Rust language.</s> <s>A developer found the change cut start-up time by about ten percent on Linux.</s> <s>When agentic tools spawn thousands of small processes, shaving milliseconds off each one is a real bet on speed, and it nudges the wider ecosystem to follow.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>